Platinium by Cycl0o0
====================

Platinium is a de-Googled fork of Chromium.
Homepage: https://platinium.cyclooo.fr

LICENSING
---------
This project is a *combined work* of two license regimes. Read this carefully,
because you cannot place all of Platinium under a single license:

1. Upstream Chromium and its third-party components remain under their
   ORIGINAL licenses — chiefly the BSD 3-Clause License (see ./LICENSE) plus
   the many licenses catalogued by `chrome://credits`. The BSD license
   REQUIRES that the upstream copyright notices be retained; they have been.
   You may not relicense that code under the AGPL.

2. The Platinium-specific additions authored by Cycl0o0 are licensed under the
   GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (see ./LICENSE.platinium). This
   covers, non-exhaustively:
     - branding assets (chrome/app/theme/chromium/* replaced by Platinium art,
       icon set, BRANDING file changes, product-name strings),
     - the de-Google build configuration,
     - the Platinium MCP <-> CDP bridge (~/platinium-mcp),
     - the bundled OpenDeezer control extension,
     - the GPTerminal interoperability configuration,
     - any other file added or modified by Cycl0o0 and marked as such.

Because the AGPL-covered layer runs as part of / alongside the browser and can
be network-accessed (the MCP bridge), the AGPL's network-use clause (section
13) applies to those components: if you offer Platinium's AGPL parts to users
over a network, you must offer them the corresponding source.

WHY NOT "AGPL FOR EVERYTHING"
-----------------------------
The user asked for "AGPL 3.0 si disponible" (if possible). It is possible for
Cycl0o0's own code, and that is what is done here. It is NOT legally possible
for the Chromium codebase itself, which is BSD-licensed by The Chromium
Authors and includes GPL-incompatible and separately-licensed third-party
code. Dual-tracking (BSD upstream + AGPL additions) is the correct and honest
arrangement.

